## 2. Empirical Record & Solver Evolution

* **Real-World Calibration:** Evaluated against real NOAA DART station 21418 records of the 2011 Tohoku event (maximum de-tided deep-ocean residual of $1.874\text{ m}$; deep-water dynamic pressure under test $\sim 3.1\text{ Pa}$)[span_1](start_span)[span_1](end_span).
* **Solver Progression:** Initial 1D MUSCL-Rusanov and Lax-Friedrichs shallow-water solvers (entries 3/5) were upgraded to **SSP-RK2** after a forward-Euler weak instability was caught on long waves (entry 8)[span_2](start_span)[span_2](end_span). Grids are converged under $1-2\%$ at halved spatial step $dx$[span_3](start_span)[span_3](end_span).
* **Lattice Configuration:** Modeled as a porous zone with bulk quadratic drag ($C_d = 0.01/\text{m}$, representing dense pile-field density)[span_4](start_span)[span_4](end_span).

